l distinguishes two required reads from one. Throw-cancel control distinguishes local done true/false AND contains one uncaught upstream disposal error; it is not a clean assertion-only control or a timeout. Source restoration is producer-attributed, with current native bytes verified. Prior twelve-test/current one-test runs and surviving/inconclusive controls remain separately qualified; no current gate/Worker/browser/provider/audio acceptance is claimed.\n\nThis fulfills correction preparation feedback only. No checker source execution, edits, private probes or new tests occurred. Original normal Git W1 d3f84ff6b9c120c30afb60f942a0bf8bb4eabb25/c6a48af403168784d8bd7f56860c8c9d7f317bc1, final gate, formal Source review and landing remain open. Live-interface design and F1 generic authority work remain separate.","body":{"metadata_verdict":"one-residual-consistency-correction-needed","promise":"06672da832da1e3192ef4debf456bea91d6b14ac","source_head":"468cd797255288c662c21b1324f5375680dd0353","source_tree":"14233b9ce7efbc1c04ea7c13728e96a1b48d6e69"}}